        '3-5', $q$A Weather Station in Every Class$q$, $q$(1) Right now, our class checks the weather on the computer each morning. (2) Every classroom at Riverside School should have its own small weather station. (3) A weather station has tools like a thermometer, a rain gauge, and a wind vane.

(4) Students would learn science by reading these tools. (5) For instance, they could measure how much rain fell overnight. (6) Students could also practice math. (7) They could make graphs of the temperature each day and compare the weeks. (8) The weather was cloudy and gray yesterday. (9) In addition, weather stations make learning feel real. (10) Kids care more about facts they collect with their own hands.$q$, 'draft')
